course: dictionary
lesson: 301
title: Words from the doctor's chair
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some medical words look hard, but the words around them give clues. «For a filling the dentist numbs the tooth with a local anaesthetic injection.» Numbs tells you the tooth stops feeling, so an anaesthetic is something that stops you feeling. Try your meaning in the sentence: "the dentist stops the tooth feeling with a medicine" makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: There are two kinds. A local anaesthetic numbs only one small part of the body, like a tooth or a lip. A general anaesthetic makes you sleep through the whole operation, so you feel nothing at all. «Before a general anaesthetic the stomach must be empty» tells you the general kind affects the whole body, because the patient is fully asleep.
explain: Anaesthetic can also be an adjective, a describing word. «An anaesthetic cream» is a cream that causes loss of feeling, so the skin goes numb. When a word has more than one job, check which job it does in the sentence: is it a thing (a noun) or a describing word (an adjective)?
fact: An anaesthetic is a medicine that stops you feeling pain.
fact: A local anaesthetic numbs one part of the body; a general anaesthetic makes you sleep through the whole operation.
fact: «As the anaesthetic wears off, children may feel sleepy, sick or muddled.» Wears off means it slowly stops working.
fact: As an adjective, anaesthetic describes something that causes loss of feeling, such as «an anaesthetic cream».
fact: Doctors and dentists give anaesthetics before operations and treatments, and an anaesthetist watches over the patient.
exercise: What does an anaesthetic do? | Helps you run faster | *Stops you feeling pain | Makes you grow taller | Makes you feel pain more strongly
exercise: «For a filling the dentist numbs the tooth with a local anaesthetic.» What does local mean here? | Loud and noisy | *Only one small part of the body | Done by a local shop | Affecting the whole body
exercise: «Before a general anaesthetic the stomach must be empty, so food can't come up.» What is a general anaesthetic? | A tiny injection in a finger | *A medicine that makes you sleep through the whole operation | A cream for a sore knee | A lunch for patients
test: «As the anaesthetic wears off, children may feel sleepy, sick or muddled.» What does wears off mean? | Is poured onto the skin | Gets stronger and stronger | Starts to work | *Slowly stops working
test: Which word describes something that causes loss of feeling, as in «an anaesthetic cream»? | Cream | Operation | Medicine | *Anaesthetic
exam: Tom's lip is still numb after a filling, and he is told not to chew it. What is the best explanation? | The anaesthetic wore off straight away and he felt fine | Lips never feel anything after eating | *A local anaesthetic numbs only a small part, and feeling can take a few hours to return | The dentist gave him a general anaesthetic, so he is still asleep
